.TH CYAML_NODE_TAG 3 "2026-08-17" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_node_tag \- return a node's YAML tag
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

const char *cyaml_node_tag(cyaml node);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Return node's YAML tag, or NULL if it carries none.

A node parsed from a document with an explicit tag ("!!str", a custom
"!foo", or a %TAG-resolved shorthand/verbatim tag) carries the fully
resolved tag string here: one of the seven CYAML_TAG_* constants
(CYAML_TAG_NULL, _BOOL, _INT, _FLOAT, _STR, _SEQ, _MAP), or a custom
tag string.  An untagged node, including one whose type was
determined purely by implicit core-schema resolution, returns NULL.

A dictionary key can never carry a tag: this DOM's keys are plain
strings, not nodes (see cyaml_dictionary_get(3)), so a tag decorating
a key is parsed for validity but has nowhere to be stored and is
discarded.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
node  DOM node handle; may be NULL (returns NULL).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Borrowed, non-owning tag string, or NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_node_set_tag (3),
.BR cyaml_type (3),
.BR cyaml_dictionary_get (3)
